From 515346f62b3993574313ccf6c4f130351ac8baf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 13:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qb64pe: include kernel/image.h before the Haiku GUI headers

Haiku's BArchivable.h uses image_id in instantiate_object() without defining
it; pulling in <kernel/image.h> first makes gui.cpp compile.
---
 qb64pe/internal/c/parts/gui/gui.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/qb64pe/internal/c/parts/gui/gui.cpp b/qb64pe/internal/c/parts/gui/gui.cpp
index 009ad4cc8..bce4fbd75 100644
--- a/qb64pe/internal/c/parts/gui/gui.cpp
+++ b/qb64pe/internal/c/parts/gui/gui.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@
 // QB64_HAIKU is defined by libqb-common.h, which the include above pulls in,
 // so the Haiku GUI headers have to come after it.
 #ifdef QB64_HAIKU
+// Haiku's BArchivable declares instantiate_object(..., image_id*) and does not
+// pull in the definition of image_id itself, so kernel/image.h must come first.
+#    include <kernel/image.h>
 #    include <Alert.h>
 #    include <InterfaceDefs.h>
 #endif
-- 
